  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "I'm running a VM with Fedora Commons 3.4.2 and Mulgara 2.1.4 . I want to use the latest functionality of Mulgara, which is now at 2.1.13.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "What I did was:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "renamed mulgara-core-2.1.4.jar to mulgara-core-2.1.4.jar.backup",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "deployed the latest files to the lib folder ( /usr/local/fedora/tomcat/webapps/fedora/WEB-INF/lib )",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "restarted Fedora (tomcat)",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      }
     ],
     "type": "bulletList"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "After that I saw that the Fedora java processes were running but I couldn't access Fedora.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Has anyone tried this before? Any tips or ideas?",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
