       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/94858ef66c252d2ebbc0ee4b97c8108a?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDJ-6.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Danny Joris",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A09c4b091-d44d-4d9e-9924-126437e1063b",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>The reason why I want to upgrade is because I need recent SPARQL functionality: <a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/9282846/sparql-combining-variables-with-literals\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://stackoverflow.com/questions/9282846/sparql-combining-variables-with-literals</a></p>\n\n<p>I got in touch with Paul Gearon and he told me I had to rewrite the code a bit:<br/>\nSELECT * WHERE {<br/>\n  $object dc:identifier $identifier .<br/>\n  LET ($new := IRI(fn:concat(str($object), \"/MODS\")))<br/>\n  $new fedora-view:disseminationType $mods .<br/>\n  $new fedora-view:disseminationType $tn .<br/>\n}</p>\n\n<p>IRI isn't recognized by Mulgara 2.1.4 , so I need an upgrade.</p>\n\n<p>Being able to do optional checks would save us so much time on page loads. I'm using Islandora.</p>",
     "created": "15/Feb/12 5:54 PM",
