  "description": "<p>I'm running a VM with Fedora Commons 3.4.2 and Mulgara 2.1.4 . I want to use the latest functionality of Mulgara, which is now at 2.1.13.<br/>\nWhat I did was:</p>\n<ul class=\"alternate\" type=\"square\">\n\t<li>renamed mulgara-core-2.1.4.jar to mulgara-core-2.1.4.jar.backup</li>\n\t<li>deployed the latest files to the lib folder ( /usr/local/fedora/tomcat/webapps/fedora/WEB-INF/lib )</li>\n\t<li>restarted Fedora (tomcat)</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<p>After that I saw that the Fedora java processes were running but I couldn't access Fedora.</p>\n\n<p>Has anyone tried this before? Any tips or ideas?</p>",
